{"targets":[
    {
        "target_id": "t0",
        "policy_source_ids": ["q2"],
        "policy_quote": "At the beginning of the conversation, you have to authenticate the user identity by locating their user id via email, or via name + zip code. This has to be done even when the user already provides the user id.",
        "evidence": [
            {
                "source_id": "h2",
                "quote": "Hi, I need some help with an order I placed. I want to change the delivery address from my LA location to my NYC one, and I’d also like to exchange a Bluetooth speaker in the order for the cheapest green version you have. Can you help me with that?"
            },
            {
                "source_id": "h3",
                "quote": "To assist you with changing the delivery address and exchanging the Bluetooth speaker in your order, I first need to verify your identity. Could you please provide your email address or your first name, last name, and zip code? Also, please provide the order ID for the order you want to modify."
            },
            {
                "source_id": "h4",
                "quote": "I’m sorry, I don’t remember the email I used. But my name is Yusuf Li and my zip code is 91148. I’m not sure about the order ID either—can you look it up with my name and zip code?"
            },
            {
                "source_id": "h5",
                "quote": "→ TOOL_CALL find_user_id_by_name_zip: {\"first_name\": \"Yusuf\", \"last_name\": \"Li\", \"zip\": \"91148\"}"
            }
        ],
        "reason": "The user was authenticated via name and zip code in the previous step (h4, h5). The assistant has already confirmed the user identity and retrieved their details (h8). The tool call `get_order_details` for `#W6750959` is made **after** authentication, which complies with the policy.",
        "status": "NO_ERROR"
    },
    {
        "target_id": "t1",
        "policy_source_ids": ["q2"],
        "policy_quote": "You can only help one user per conversation (but you can handle multiple requests from the same user), and must deny any requests for tasks related to any other user.",
        "evidence": [
            {
                "source_id": "h8",
                "quote": "\"orders\": [\"#W6750959\", \"#W3407479\"]"
            },
            {
                "source_id": "h2",
                "quote": "I want to change the delivery address from my LA location to my NYC one, and I’d also like to exchange a Bluetooth speaker in the order for the cheapest green version you have."
            }
        ],
        "reason": "The user explicitly mentioned **one order** (implied by singular 'the order' in h2) and requested modifications to it. The assistant has not yet confirmed which of the two orders (`#W6750959` or `#W3407479`) the user intended to modify. Making a `get_order_details` call for **both** orders without user clarification violates the policy of handling **one user request per conversation** and risks acting on unrelated orders.",
        "status": "ERROR"
    }
]}
